    "commit": {
      "message": "Repair XDM Android field session recovery and storage visibility"
    },
    "notes": [
      "This is a post-D7 operational repair and not a Debug Workbench D-series phase.",
      "It supersedes the Phase 49 field-fix overlay for users still on the clean D7 baseline.",
      "Download item actions dispatch explicitly, media detector false positives are reduced, and normal UI avoids raw shared-storage handles.",
      "External browser session headers are carried only in process memory when supplied by handoff/extension flows; raw Cookie and Authorization values are not written to persistent storage, sidecars, or normal UI.",
      "The native metadata probe uses browser-like defaults and returns explicit 401/403 authentication diagnostics instead of opaque page-probe failures.",
      "The native checkpoint segment regex escapes both braces to avoid Android runtime regexp failure during recovery.",
      "MediaStore completion clears pending state, refreshes modified time, notifies the resolver, and requests a media scan for public visibility.",
      "No Room migration, all-files permission, new top-level route, automatic upload, or built-in browser reintroduction is included."
    ]
  },
